# USQ - Restore a squeezed file

```text
USQ [drive:]file [destination-drive:]
```

## Restore a file

```text
B0:USQ A:NOTES.TQT D:
```

USQ reads the original name from the squeezed header, checks the stored
checksum and writes NOTES.TXT on D. An existing file of that name blocks
restoration. The compressed input stays in place.

## Restore help text

```text
B0:USQ A:PIP.HQP D:
```

This makes the [SQ](SQ.HLP) version editable again. HELP can also read a
.HQP directly. For a crunched .HZP use [UNCR](UNCR.HLP).
